   "kryhin_sudhir_2023": "arXiv:2309.09105 (PRL 134, 061501): Eq. 6 = epsilon x Diosi kernel; Eq. 8 \"L_G ~ -epsilon G m1 m2/(hbar R^3)[x1,[x2,rho]]\"; proposes measuring S_x1x2 (\"anti-correlated motion away from resonance, accompanied by a characteristic phase shift\"). NOTE: direct expansion of their Eq. 6 with both x along +axis gives +2 epsilon G m1 m2/(hbar R^3)[x1,[x2,rho]] (our -2 G hbar/d^3); their Eq. 8 has half the magnitude and opposite sign (their main-text H_G = G m1 m2 x1 x2/(2R^3) is also 4x below the K = 2Gm1m2/R^3 used in their appendix mu). Absorbed in their free epsilon; sign depends on axis convention - flagged, not resolved.",
