  "caveats": [
   "ASSUMED: the state-dependent kernel uses the TOTAL smeared mass density m(x) (field-theory reading, as in Oppenheim Eq. 46 where the decoherence rate of a body ~ M_lambda m_P/(l_P^3 D2), i.e. its own bulk density). Stage 27 used the isolated nucleus.",
   "ASSUMED: simple-cubic lattice with a = (m/rho)^(1/3) for liquid Xe in the crossover l ~ a.",
   "OPEN: for l > a neighbouring nuclei receive strongly correlated kicks; collective X-ray emission was not modelled (same open point applies to the Stage 26 DP X-ray mapping for l > a).",
   "LPF self-term only (spacecraft/housing masses would add matter-sourced noise -> tighter Dhat_max); cube treated as equal-volume sphere."
  ],
  "literature": {
   "oppenheim_2023": "arXiv:2203.01982 Sec. V / App. F: \"the discrete models appear less constrained due to the suppression of the noise away from the mass density ... <D2(x,y,Phi)> = (l_P^3/m_P) D2 m(x)\" and the torsion/Cavendish squeeze \"10^-1 kg s >= (l_P^3/m_P) D2 >= 10^-25 kg s\" - matter-sourced noise and its test with source-mass (Cavendish) experiments already in the paper.",
   "carney_taylor_2023": "arXiv:2301.08378 (\"Strongly incoherent gravity\"): noise sourced by a source mass, Gamma_incoh = G^2 M m^2 l^2 sigma^2/(d^6 v^2), and \"the entire remaining parameter space can be tested by looking for loss of quantum coherence in small systems like atom interferometers coupled to oscillating source masses\" - modulated-source-mass test of matter-sourced classical-gravity noise."
  }
 },
 "verdicts": {
  "claim1": {
   "verdict": "CONFIRMED numerically for spheres/cubes; ALREADY KNOWN (Diosi 1989/2007; NHH 2014 Eq. 11; volume signature in Oppenheim 2023); CORRECTED in scope",
   "value": 2.948291933255009e-44,
   "ratio": 0.9999999773129693,
   "corrections": [
    "shape: Gamma_ii V = 4 pi G hbar (kappa+1/4kappa) N_ii (demagnetization tensor); claim exact only for N = 1/3 (sphere, cube)",
    "composition/mass independence only for homogeneous bodies; general V -> V_eff = M^2/int rho^2",
    "finite l/R deficit (see finite_l_over_R); lattice correction < 1e-30 at l >= 4.5 A"
   ]
  },
  "claim2": {
   "verdict": "CONFIRMED (-2.000, +1.000 G hbar/d^3 at kappa=1/2); ALREADY KNOWN (Gaona-Reyes et al. 2021 Eq. 47; Kryhin-Sudhir 2023 Eq. 6/8); CORRECTED wording; Stage 27 KTM attribution WRONG",
   "corrections": [
    "magnitude is -2 G hbar (kappa+1/4kappa)/d^3 >= 2 G hbar/d^3, not kappa-independent; only rho is kappa-independent and only in the DP family",
    "KTM (LOCC) predicts rho = 0; TD with local gamma predicts zero longitudinal correlation -> the sign/axis pattern discriminates kernels (useful, and the one framing we did not find stated)"
   ]
